  <p class="text-lg">
    A from-scratch electric go kart build — my first major hands-on engineering project. 
    Designed in Fusion 360 and fabricated using shop tools and flux-cored arc welding.
  </p>

  <h2>The Build</h2>
  <p>
    This was a personal project that got me hooked on building things. I designed the frame 
    in Fusion 360, then fabricated it using flux-cored arc welding (FCAW) and general shop 
    tools. The project covered the full build cycle from CAD design through to a running vehicle.
  </p>

  <h2>What I Learned</h2>
  <p>
    This project was my introduction to the overlap between design and fabrication — learning 
    that what looks good in CAD doesn't always work in the real world. It taught me welding 
    fundamentals, basic electrical systems, and the importance of iterating when things don't 
    go according to plan.
  </p>
